    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“Some people break things by accident. You do it on the paperwork <strong>and</strong> the map on purpose.”</em></p><p><strong>Primary Ability:</strong> Strength</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> Siege-born demolisher who turns walls, dogmas, and bad ideas into usable rubble.</p><p>Breakers are the shock-corps of the Great Work: armored saints of structural failure. Where they walk, bastions crack, bunkers remember they were once caves, and the world’s worst architecture finally gets the performance review it deserves.</p><h3>Class Features by Tier</h3><p><em>(These are BBTTCC “tiers” that sit on top of normal level-by-level class progression.)</em></p><ul><li><p><strong>Tier 1 — Certified Structural Menace.</strong><br />You gain proficiency in <em>Athletics</em> and <em>Mason’s Tools</em>. When you damage or attempt to destroy nonmagical structures, you ignore any resistance they might have to your damage. Your faction’s <strong>Violence OP cap increases by 3</strong> as Command starts budgeting for “Breaker-class solutions.”</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 2 — Siege Cost Accountant.</strong><br />When your faction initiates a <em>Siege</em> operation, the Violence OP cost for that activity is reduced by <strong>1</strong> (minimum 0), as long as you are present in the operation or clearly responsible for the plan on paper.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 3 — Ruin to Renewal.</strong><br />When you destroy a fortification, barricade, or other significant defensive structure, you can attempt to turn the moment of collapse into an act of reclamation. Make either a Faith-based or Economy-based ability check (your choice) against DC 15, keyed to your GM’s preferred skill (such as Religion, Insight, Persuasion, or tools that fit the scene). On a success, the ground and people around the ruin shift toward healing: lingering badness is purified, a hex status improves, or your faction gains a small narrative boon as appropriate.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 4 — Architect of Endings.</strong><br />Your faction has learned to ride the shockwaves you create. <strong>Violence Attrition penalties are halved</strong> for your faction (rounding in your favor) for conflicts and operations in which you participate, representing smarter de-escalation, cleaner victories, and fewer “oops, we toppled the entire province” incidents.</p></li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
